THE 10-SECOND MASSAGE — third-party material

MUSIC
- Frédéric Chopin, Nocturne in E-flat major, Op. 9 No. 2 (composition: public domain).
  Recording: "Musopen – The Complete Works of Frédéric Chopin" (Musopen Kickstarter project, 2012), dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.
  Source: https://archive.org/details/musopen-chopin-complete-works-flac  (file "Nocturne in E flat major, Op. 9 no. 2.flac"; build.sh fetches it)
  Edited in mix.py: the opening theme (0:00–0:16), suspended at the husband's freeze; the end of the first statement and the
  ornamented second statement (from 0:28, the second statement exactly under the ten-second massage); a fragment of the final
  cadenza under "There you go, honey!", cut mid-phrase on the wife's stare. Level-ridden for small speakers.

VOICES
- ElevenLabs text to speech, model Eleven v4, generated on the film owner's ElevenLabs account (one clip per line, two takes each,
  every take checked with faster-whisper small.en). Voices (voice IDs):
  HIM (the husband) — "Hurker – Confident, Playful & Warm" (AgWmGPmoY5bWqnxOVd0j)
  HER (the wife)    — "Jessica – Playful, Bright, Warm" (cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9)
  Takes used: audio/sessions.tsv. Use of the generated audio is governed by the account holder's ElevenLabs plan and terms.

SOUND EFFECTS
- All synthesised in mix.py (original): room tone, birdsong and the bird's chirp, footsteps, couch creaks, cushion settles,
  fabric rubs of the massage, pats, the sleeve tug, breaths, hoodie stretch. Built with the Lemo-Opuscar foley helpers (MIT).

